# Old addresses. Every rule here is a 200 rewrite: the old address serves the
# page for the same thing, and that page keeps its own canonical tag, so search
# engines fold the old address into it. Nothing here redirects (Sarth: long-lived
# URLs are worth keeping, so the old ones always answer). The only redirect on
# the site is the Worker's host and protocol hop to https://www.sarth.net.
# build.py --check fails on any rule that is not a 200 to a page that exists.
# Redirects win over files, so never list a path that has its own page in public/.
# A post that came back as a page lives at its old address and needs no rule;
# slashless forms of those get the assets' trailing-slash normalization.

